    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταστῠγ-έω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέστῠγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.694
				</span></i>
			:—<i>to be horror-struck</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέστυγε μῦθον ἀκούσας</span> l.c.: c.acc.,
				<i>abhor, abominate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ δ᾽ ἔστυγον αὐτήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.113
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόρπα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					476
				</span></i>
			: later aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεστύγησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>VS</u>
					p.471
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέστυγε</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> causal in
				aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέστυξα</span>, <i>make abominable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				731.26
			</span></i> (but in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισῆσαι</span>
			). pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεστυγημένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phot.
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; f.l. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μένως</span>
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
